  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25596016",
      "title": "Adding Two-Way Binding",
      "sourceHash": "bfd6d4223d0d3669bb7cd01cc721b9a797487670b2d6b08ce6a2559a7fcfc1ea",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.066,
          "end": 5.8,
          "en": "Instructor: How can we clear those inputs?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.8,
          "end": 8.2,
          "en": "Well, that's part of the reason why I wanted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.2,
          "end": 12.7,
          "en": "to use state for storing the entered values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.7,
          "end": 15.066,
          "en": "We could've also used the global variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.066,
          "end": 16.8,
          "en": "outside of the component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.8,
          "end": 20.633,
          "en": "Otherwise, if we just wanted to persist the values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.633,
          "end": 23.766,
          "en": "but by using state, we have an advantage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.766,
          "end": 25.666,
          "en": "We can now implement something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.666,
          "end": 28.833,
          "en": "which is called two-way binding, which simply means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.833,
          "end": 30.6,
          "en": "which is called two-way binding, which simply means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.6,
          "end": 35.166,
          "en": "that for inputs we don't just listen to changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.166,
          "end": 40,
          "en": "but we can also pass a new value back into the input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40,
          "end": 44.633,
          "en": "So that we can reset or change the input programmatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.633,
          "end": 47.666,
          "en": "And how do we do that? Well, it's very simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.666,
          "end": 51.3,
          "en": "All we have to do is add the value attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.3,
          "end": 56.333,
          "en": "which is a default attribute, to this input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.333,
          "end": 59.133,
          "en": "This will set the internal value property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.133,
          "end": 61.2,
          "en": "which every input element has.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.2,
          "end": 64.3,
          "en": "And we can set it to a new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.3,
          "end": 69.066,
          "en": "And here, I will bind this to enteredTitle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 69.066,
          "end": 71.166,
          "en": "So now it is this two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.166,
          "end": 71.2,
          "en": "So now it is this two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.2,
          "end": 73.733,
          "en": "because now we don't just listen to changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.733,
          "end": 76.366,
          "en": "in the input to update our state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.366,
          "end": 79.733,
          "en": "But we also feed the state back into the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.733,
          "end": 83.633,
          "en": "so that when we change the state, we also change input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.633,
          "end": 85.46600000000001,
          "en": "This might sound like an infinite loop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.46600000000001,
          "end": 86.533,
          "en": "but it actually isn't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.533,
          "end": 89.3,
          "en": "So we won't have a problem there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.3,
          "end": 91.833,
          "en": "But the advantage is that when the form is submitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.833,
          "end": 93.5,
          "en": "for example, we can call setEnteredTitle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.5,
          "end": 97.6,
          "en": "for example, we can call setEnteredTitle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.6,
          "end": 100.566,
          "en": "And set this back to an empty string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.566,
          "end": 103.833,
          "en": "which also was our initial state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.833,
          "end": 107.5,
          "en": "And by doing that, we override what the user entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.5,
          "end": 109.43299999999999,
          "en": "after the form was submitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.43299999999999,
          "end": 111.733,
          "en": "and therefore cleared the input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.733,
          "end": 112.366,
          "en": "and therefore cleared the input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.366,
          "end": 114.6,
          "en": "And we can do this for all inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 114.6,
          "end": 117.7,
          "en": "We can set the entered amount to an empty string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.7,
          "end": 123.466,
          "en": "and set the entered date to an empty string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.466,
          "end": 128.2,
          "en": "and then just add to the value prop to all these inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.2,
          "end": 128.4,
          "en": "and then just add to the value prop to all these inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.4,
          "end": 132.066,
          "en": "So here I add value and point at enteredAmount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.066,
          "end": 135.033,
          "en": "to pass that back into the amount input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.033,
          "end": 137.9,
          "en": "And do the same here for the date,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 137.9,
          "end": 138.03300000000002,
          "en": "And do the same here for the date,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.03300000000002,
          "end": 142.766,
          "en": "pass the entered date back into the input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 142.766,
          "end": 148.433,
          "en": "If we now save that and I reload, this is looking good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.433,
          "end": 153.2,
          "en": "Now, we can still enter something here as it seems,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.2,
          "end": 155.266,
          "en": "but if I click Add Expense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.266,
          "end": 157.733,
          "en": "you'll see it's all cleared again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.733,
          "end": 159.633,
          "en": "And we still have our data collected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.633,
          "end": 161.966,
          "en": "and stored here in this object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.966,
          "end": 164.8,
          "en": "So this is a neat behavior, but more importantly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.8,
          "end": 168.03300000000002,
          "en": "this is also another key concept in React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.03300000000002,
          "end": 168.166,
          "en": "this is also another key concept in React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 168.166,
          "end": 170.633,
          "en": "Two-way binding is very useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 170.633,
          "end": 172.633,
          "en": "when you're working with forms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 172.633,
          "end": 175.333,
          "en": "because it allows you to gather user input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 175.333,
          "end": 176.86599999999999,
          "en": "but then also change it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 176.86599999999999,
          "end": 179.4,
          "en": "For example, upon form of mission.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
